title: Lio
act: Survey
location: Mill
scenario: The moving stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: not $saw_lio
---
Lio: You're the map maker. Can I see? Just the edge?
Lio: I make maps too. Of the mill, and the river. Grandmother taught me. She knew where everything was before.
Lio: The loft has the best view. You can see the whole bend of the river from up there.
===

title: Lio
act: Survey
location: Mill
scenario: The moving stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $saw_lio and $culprit == Culprit.Unknown
---
Lio: You saw me. Last night. Are you going to tell Maren?
Lio: I'm not stealing land. I'm putting the stones back where they were. Grandmother said the true line runs under the hill, where the lantern folk are.
Lio: Nobody believes her, because she's dead.
-> Who are the lantern folk?
    Lio: Lights, deep in the mine. The miners say so. Grandmother said they are the old border, written down.
-> You can't go on moving them.
    Lio: Then somebody should draw them where they belong.
===

title: Lio
act: Survey
location: Mill
scenario: The moving stones
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $culprit != Culprit.Unknown
---
<<if $culprit == Culprit.Lio>>
    Lio: Maren came. Father shouted. The stones stay where they are now. #mood:angry
<<else>>
    Lio: They took the peddler in. Because of me. I didn't ask you to lie. #mood:sad
<<endif>>
===

title: Loft
act: All
location: Mill
quest: survey
---
<<if surveyed("loft")>>
    The loft is on your map. The river bends below, silver and slow.
<<else>>
    You climb the ladder into the loft. From the hatch you see the whole bend of the river, and the stones along it.
    <<survey loft>>
    <<detour SurveyCheck>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Sacks
act: All
location: Mill
scenario: The road
---
<<if $wheel_mended>>
    Sacks of fresh flour, still warm from the stones.
<<else>>
    Empty sacks. The mill has not ground for a week.
<<endif>>
===

title: Nan
act: Survey
location: Cottage
quest: herbs
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $quest_herbs == QuestState.NotStarted
---
Nan: Close the door, the warmth is getting out. I'm Nan. I make what the valley needs when it is ill.
Nan: I'm short of three herbs for the spring. Nettle from the green, a dew-cup from the river, and hollyroot. Hedda has some in her cellar wall, though she doesn't know it.
Nan: The dew-cup only opens in the morning, mind. And not for long now. Two mornings more, at most.
-> I will bring them.
    Nan: Good. I'll make you something for your trouble.
    <<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Active>>
-> I have a map to make.
    Nan: So you do. The herbs will wait. The dew-cups won't.
    <<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Offered>>
<<quest_changed herbs>>
===

title: Nan
act: All
location: Cottage
quest: herbs
when: $quest_herbs == QuestState.Offered
---
Nan: Changed your mind about my herbs?
-> Yes. Nettle, dew-cup, hollyroot.
    Nan: You were listening. Go on, then.
    <<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed herbs>>
-> Not yet.
===

title: Nan
act: All
location: Cottage
quest: herbs
when: $quest_herbs == QuestState.Active
---
<<if has_item("nettle") and has_item("dewcup") and has_item("hollyroot")>>
    Nan: All three. And the dew-cup still wet. You have a good hand.
    <<take nettle>>
    <<take dewcup>>
    <<take hollyroot>>
    Nan: Here. A remedy against the cold. Drink it before cold water, and the water won't stop your heart.
    Nan: I don't know why a map maker would need it. But you will go places I don't.
    <<give remedy>>
    <<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed herbs>>
<<else>>
    Nan: Still missing [plural value={3 - item_count("nettle") - item_count("dewcup") - item_count("hollyroot")} one="one herb" other="% herbs" /].
<<endif>>
===

title: Nan
act: All
location: Cottage
scenario: The moving stones
when: $quest_herbs != QuestState.Offered and $quest_herbs != QuestState.Active
when: $quest_herbs != QuestState.NotStarted or $act != Act.Survey
---
=> Nan: Lio's grandmother and I picked herbs together for forty years. She knew every stone in this valley.
=> Nan: The castle's steward came for a sleeping draught last month. I didn't ask what for.
=> Nan: You'll take a cold down there in the mine, if you go. Everyone does. <<if $act == Act.Castle>>
===

title: HerbTable
act: All
location: Cottage
quest: herbs
---
Jars and bunches on the table, each with a label in Nan's tidy hand. One jar is labelled "for the deep cold".
===

title: Bell
act: All
location: Chapel
quest: survey
---
<<if surveyed("bell")>>
    The bell tower is on your map. The rope sways a little in the draught.
<<else>>
    You climb the tower beside the bell rope. From the top the whole valley lies open, the castle, the mine, the abbey's meadows.
    You take your bearings from the bell itself.
    <<survey bell>>
    <<detour SurveyCheck>>
<<endif>>
===

title: MasonMark
act: All
location: Chapel
scenario: The moving stones
---
A mason's mark cut in the wall: a circle with a line through it, the same as on the boundary stones by the river.
<<once>>
    Under it, almost worn away, words in the old tongue. "As above, so under the hill."
<<endonce>>
===
